EXT. DRIVING TEST CENTRE - SNOWY PARKING LOT - DAY

Flurries. A small hatchback idles at a cone. The wipers beat.

MILLICENT OYELOWO-FARR, 17, white-knuckled at the wheel. In the passenger seat, an EXAMINER, 50s, thick coat, clipboard, a face that gave up expecting surprises.

EXAMINER
Signal left.

MILLICENT
Left.

She flips the signal. Wrong direction.

EXAMINER
Your other left.

She switches. The car creeps forward.

EXAMINER (CONT'D)
Slower.

MILLICENT
I'm barely moving.

EXAMINER
Slower than barely.

The car rolls three feet and stops.

MILLICENT
Done.

EXAMINER
That's the parking lot.

MILLICENT
I know.

The Examiner writes something. She watches the pen.

MILLICENT (CONT'D)
What are you writing?

EXAMINER
Weather observations.

MILLICENT
Is that on the form?

EXAMINER
It's on my form.

She exhales. The wipers beat. Snow collects on the glass.

MILLICENT
What's your name?

EXAMINER
It's on the badge.

MILLICENT
It's turned around.

He looks down. Flips the badge.

BOGDAN
Bogdan.

MILLICENT
Bogdan. I'm Millicent.

BOGDAN
I know. It's on my form.

MILLICENT
Did I pass?

BOGDAN
You parked.

MILLICENT
Is that a yes?

BOGDAN
It's a yes if you shut off the engine.

She reaches for the key. Hesitates.

MILLICENT
Can I just sit here a minute?

Bogdan puts his clipboard on the dashboard. Leans back.

BOGDAN
Take your time. It's snowing.
